      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "`Backup.zipExtract` writes each entry of the chosen backup ZIP to `new File(targetDir, zipEntry.getName())` without checking where that path ends up. An entry name containing `../` resolves outside `targetDir`, so a crafted or corrupted backup file could overwrite other files of the app when it is restored (the usual \"Zip Slip\" pattern).\n\nThis change resolves the canonical path of the restore folder and of each entry, and skips any entry that would land outside it. Backups made by the app itself only contain plain file names, so restoring them works as before.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
